From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Kling <webgeek1234@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 17:36:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add cpu OPP table with DDR and LLCC
 bandwidths

Add the OPP tables for each CPU cluster (cpu0-1-2-3-4-5 & cpu6-7) to
permit scaling the Last Level Cache Controller (LLCC) and DDR frequency
by aggregating bandwidth requests of all CPU core with reference to the
current OPP they are configured in by the hardware.

The effect is proper caches & DDR frequency scaling when CPU cores
change frequency.

The OPP tables were built using the downstream memlat ddr & llcc tables
for each cluster types with the actual cpufreq LUT tables from running a
CQ8725S device.

Also add the interconnect entry for each cpu, with 2 different paths:
- CPU to Last Level Cache Controller (LLCC)
- Last Level Cache Controller (LLCC) to DDR

Signed-off-by: Aaron Kling <webgeek1234@gmail.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260605-sm8750-ddr-bw-scaling-v1-1-f39f918c95a7@gmail.com
[ROCKNIX: vote LLCC frequencies on the CPU to LLCC path and DDR frequencies
 on the LLCC to EBI path, as the SM8750 vendor qcom,dcvs nodes do (LLCC:
 gem_noc APPSS to LLCC, bus-width 16; DDR: mc_virt LLCC to EBI, bus-width 4);
 take each OPP's LLCC and DDR frequency from the Odin 3 vendor qcom,memlat
 tables, whose rows are ceilings (the first row at or above the CPU
 frequency applies); add the 4204800 and 4320000 kHz turbo OPPs the cpu6
 firmware reports]
